你与莱纳德的感情吗
Your relationship with Leonard?

64
00:03:12,990 --> 00:03:13,980
也不是
No.

65
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:15,290
你重回校园的失败之路吗
Your failed attempt to go back to college?

66
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:16,610
不是
No!

67
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:20,240
我是说你与弦理论就像一段感情
I'm saying you and string theory sound like a relationship,

68
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,530
而我知道那种感情的滋味
and I know what it's like to be in one

69
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:24,340
也懂那种永远不能如愿的感觉
and realize it's never gonna turn out the way you want.

70
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,110
都说是莱纳德  你还否认
I said Leonard; you said no.

71
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,800
我是指跟其他男人时啦
I'm talking about other guys.

72
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,120
好吧
Okay.

73
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,810
那你都是怎么做的
Well, what do you do?

74
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:37,120
你得有壮士断腕的勇气结束感情
You have to have the courage to end the relationship.

75
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,450
分手止损  握手道别  甩手走人
You know? Break it off, shake hands, walk away.

76
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:43,770
我不知道我能不能做到
I don't know if I can do that.

77
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:44,850
我知道这很困难  但宝贝
I know it's hard, honey,

78
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:47,430
但人都是这样成长的
but in the end, that's how you grow.

79
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:54,000
佩妮  你有看到我好的那个吸入器吗
Penny, have you seen my good inhaler?

80
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:59,170
分手止损  握手道别  甩手走人
Break it off, shake hands, walk away.

81
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,850
跟两个女人纠缠得如何啊
Hey, how's dating two women going?

82
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:09,150
遇到点小麻烦
Um, kind of hit a bump.

83
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:10,880
当我老实告诉艾米丽
When I was honest and told Emily

84
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:13,380
我同时有在与另一个人约会时  她可以接受
she wasn't the only person I was seeing, it went great.

85
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:15,380
所以我也这么告诉了露西
So I tried the same thing with Lucy.

86
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,750
然后呢
And?

87
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:19,000
她内心五味杂陈
She had mixed feelings.

88
00:04:19,990 --> 00:04:21,870
但当我说"艾米丽可以接受
But when I said, "Emily was cool with it.

89
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:24,440
艾米丽最好了  你为啥不学学艾米丽"时
Emily's the best. Why can't you be more like Emily?"...

90
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:29,290
那五味就只剩一味了
...those feelings became less mixed.

91
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:34,810
女人啊  谁知道她们不爽的点在哪
Women. Who knows what'll set 'em off?

92
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:38,470
可至少我现在能全心对一个女孩投入了
At least now I can focus all my energies on just one girl.

93
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:40,500
我希望我能尽快见到她
I hope I get to meet her as soon as possible.

94
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,370
干嘛这么着急  她又不会跑
Why the rush? She isn't going anywhere.

95
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:44,840
她会的  但我喜欢你的乐观
She is. But I like that attitude.

96
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:50,690
各位  有人对我弦理论的旧书感兴趣吗
Gentlemen, is anybody interested in my old string theory books?

97
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:52,110
你真的要这么做吗
You're really going to do this?

98
00:04:52,110 --> 00:04:54,910
是的  佩妮指出
I am. Yeah, Penny pointed out that

99
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:57,150
我现在基本上就是在经历一段分手
what I'm going through is essentially a breakup.

100
00:04:57,150 --> 00:05:00,170
而且根据《时尚》杂志中
And according to Cosmopolitan magazine,

101
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:02,530
一篇教导如何有效挥别旧爱的文章
one of the most effective techniques for moving on

102
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:05,420
分手就得丢掉会回忆起感情的一切物件
is to get rid of all reminders of the relationship.

103
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,460
-你还读起《时尚》杂志啦  -是啊
- You're reading Cosmo? - Yes.

104
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:09,830
而且我还发现  基本上
As it turns out, there's an article

105
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:13,380
每期都有教导如何挥别旧爱的文章
on how to get over a breakup in literally every issue.

106
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:15,090
反正
Anyway,

107
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:17,630
它还建议要把这些东西烧掉
it suggests that I set these on fire,

108
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,500
但烧书的味道
but the smell of burning books

109
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:23,030
会让我想起教会去德州东部野餐时的回忆
reminds me of church picnics in East Texas.

110
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:23,030
绰号为太空城的休士顿就在德州东部

111
00:05:24,690 --> 00:05:26,100
这是什么
What's this?

112
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:29,590
我随手画的超椭圆黎曼曲面而已
That's just a doodle of a hyperelliptic Riemann surface.

113
00:05:29,590 --> 00:05:32,830
这不是你当年博士后的基础吗
Oh, yeah. Wasn't that the basis of your postdoc fellowship?

114
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,110
是啊
It was.

115
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,910
当年我还觉得这很高大上
This seemed so elegant at the time,

116
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:40,660
但我现在意识到我当年只是个被
but... now I realize I was just a simple country boy

117
00:05:40,670 --> 00:05:42,910
大城市那变量都对的理论
seduced by a big city theory

118
00:05:42,910 --> 00:05:45,720
所迷惑的单纯农村小伙
with variables in all the right places.

119
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:49,570
-你会没事的  -我知道
- It's going to be okay. - I know.

120
00:05:49,570 --> 00:05:51,700
尽管很困难  我还是得挥别过去了
As hard as this is, I have to move on.

121
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:54,390
我不能再一直假定着多维度实体
I can't keep postulating multidimensional entities

122
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:56,080
却什么结果也得不到
and get nothing in return.

123
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,440
我也是有需求的人
I have needs, too.

124
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:06,170
你现在还跟艾米丽在一起吗
So, you and Emily still together?

125
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:15,450
我问过伯纳黛特了  她明天有空
I spoke to Bernadette. She's free tomorrow night.

126
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:16,500
好啊  行
Oh, okay, great.

127
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,350
但如果我们真的要四人约会
But if we're really gonna do a double date,

128
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:21,620
我们得先定下一些跟艾米丽有关的规矩
then we have to go over some ground rules about Emily.

129
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:23,770
比如最终发现她是个橡胶充气娃娃时
Like when it turns out she's made of rubber,

130
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:25,220
我啥都不许说吗
I don't say anything?

131
00:06:27,570 --> 00:06:29,040
她很真实好吗
She's very real.

132
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,400
充气娃娃盒子上都这么写啊
Oh, that's what it says on the box.

133
00:06:32,970 --> 00:06:35,410
就写在"可用洗碗机清洗"的字样旁
Right next to "Dishwasher safe."

134
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:37,490
你看
See?

135
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:38,670
我担心的就是
This is exactly the kind of thing

136
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:40,300
你在她面前说这类的话
I'm worried about you saying in front of her.

137
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:43,510
-我保证我绝对会很乖  -最好是这样
- I promise I'll be on my best behavior. - You better be.

138
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:46,070
不许开我跟我的狗很亲密的玩笑
No jokes about how close I am with my dog.

139
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,490
也不许说我跟我狗有多亲密的实话
Or the truth about how close I am with my dog.

140
00:06:50,950 --> 00:06:51,700
我保证
You got it.

141
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,650
不许开我学过一年芭蕾舞的玩笑
No jokes about the year I took ballet.

142
00:06:53,650 --> 00:06:55,570
你学过芭蕾舞吗
You took ballet?

143
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,440
天啊  你从来都不好好聆听
God, you never listen.

144
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,260
你确定你要这样吗
Are you sure you want to do this?

145
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:05,820
杂志中一篇文章建议
The magazine articles suggest that one of the ways

146
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:08,240
挥别旧情的方法就是新造型
to get over a breakup is a new look.

147
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:09,880
那你的旧造型呢
What about your old look,

148
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,500
精心打扮过的腹语术玩偶造型
well-groomed ventriloquist doll?

149
00:07:14,470 --> 00:07:17,500
-"天啊  的确是很像"  -别闹了
- "Oh, my God, I do look like that." - Stop it!

150
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,580
所以你想我怎么剪
So, how do you want me to cut it?

151
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:26,310
比尔·盖兹加尼古拉·特斯拉的发型
How about Bill Gates meets Nikola Tesla?

152
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:30,170
就是前面商人头  后面科学家头
So, business in the front, science in the back.

153
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:32,390
或者我就不剪了
Or I don't cut it

154
00:07:32,390 --> 00:07:33,890
就搞点造型就行了
and maybe just style it a little.

155
00:07:33,890 --> 00:07:35,570
你说了算
Oh, I'm in your hands.

156
00:07:35,690 --> 00:07:38,870
你弄得好我就告诉你  《时尚》教你如何轻松度过
Do a good job and I'll tell you Cosmo's ten dynamite tips

157
00:07:38,870 --> 00:07:40,870
经前症候群的10大绝招
to enjoy your PMS.

158
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:43,280
你能让他保持安静吗
Can you keep him quiet?

159
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,170
比如拿钥匙在他眼前晃
Maybe jangle some keys in front of him?

160
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:46,240
这招不好用了
That doesn't work anymore.

161
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,730
他只会觉得我是要带他去看医生
He just thinks I'm taking him to the doctor.

162
00:07:50,450 --> 00:07:52,960
所以你现在不搞弦理论了
So, now that you're no longer invested in string theory,

163
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,620
你打算研究哪方面
what are you gonna pursue?

164
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,970
有很多超有意思的领域啊
Oh, there are so many exciting areas:

165
00:07:56,970 --> 00:07:59,330
黑洞  暗物质
black holes, dark matter...

166
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:00,970
莱纳德那天还在跟我说暗物质呢
Oh, Leonard was telling me about dark matter,

167
00:08:00,970 --> 00:08:02,740
但我真的不太理解
but I didn't really understand it.

168
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:05,440
不用难过  他自己也不懂
Don't feel bad. Neither does he.

169
00:08:09,350 --> 00:08:11,120
好了
Okay...

170
00:08:11,810 --> 00:08:13,270
你觉得如何
what do you think?

171
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,710
你看没看过特斯拉的照片啊
Have you ever even seen a picture of Tesla?

172
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,710
尼古拉·特斯拉  伟大的发明家  物理学家
发型是微卷的中分头

173
